          "message": "v8.6.0 — re-pin verify v5.11.0 + EjectAggregatedTierOnly tier-granular stratum evict (§19.7.3 complete)\n\n- Re-pin all 6 CIRISVerify crates v5.10.0 → v5.11.0 (RC17 docs/compliance +\n  the EjectionVerdict::EjectAggregatedTierOnly{tier} variant).\n- Consume the new variant: EjectionAction::EjectAggregatedTierOnly(u32) +\n  the from_verdict arm; Engine::evict_aggregated_tier / Backend\n  evict_aggregated_tier_on_backend shed EXACTLY the tier-`tier`\n  content_aggregation composite's symbols (manifest survives as EnvelopeOnly),\n  leaving finer (lower-level) AND coarser (higher-level) composites intact.\n  Level-guarded (stored aggregation_level must equal tier or Ok(0) no-op);\n  composes with hard-delete (never resurrects erased content). FFI exposed.\n- Docs: EjectAggregatedTierOnly is now CONSUMED (verify v5.11.0 / persist\n  v8.6.0), not a pending follow-on. §19.7.3 surface complete.\n\nGate (independently re-run by lead after the build agent's state was lost\npre-commit): build + clippy -D + no-backend -D + fmt + nextest --all-targets\non plain postgres:16 + sqlite. Test (g): tier-1 shed → EnvelopeOnly, tier-0 +\ntier-2 stay Full, idempotent, verdict mapping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
