          "id": "08226ce2abc75d6ee0d3d1e429d0a4dcf747884b",
          "message": "v9.10.0 — #227: list_held_fountain_content (publisher-facing held enumerator) (#265)\n\nA publisher can enumerate the fountain-coded content persist holds for them\n(content_manifest.pqc_key_id) and watch it fade — the #227 \"fades but can't be\nfalsified\" property made observable without fetching symbol bytes.\n\n- Backend::list_held_fountain_content(publisher_key_id) -> Vec<FountainHeldMeta>\n  (sqlite + postgres + memory); pg reads via PgRowExt::safe_get_with. Meta =\n  manifest essentials + held_symbols (post-eviction COUNT) + recoverable\n  (held_symbols >= min_viable_symbols) + admitted_at.\n- Engine::list_held_fountain_content (pg/sqlite) + FFI list_held_fountain_content.\n- Memory parity (admitted_at empty; Engine/FFI fountain surface is pg/sqlite).\n- Tested sqlite + live pg: full -> held==n+k + recoverable; evict to T5 -> held\n  drops (fade visible) + recoverable tracks count; unknown publisher -> empty.\n\nGate: 1579/1579 nextest (full features, live pg + sqlite + memory) + clippy -D\n+ fmt + 3 no-backend combos.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RWKf675EcbswPMuEqprUNQ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-21T19:57:55-05:00",
          "tree_id": "2821d79b8fc91087bfd60c93b83bbf7fb29cd390",
