          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b840d7229868f173c26cfa2e36ac86dd7037b0a3",
          "message": "evidence(#729): publish the steward-plane and age-plane rows\n\nSix rows for symbols already shipped and unpublished, so CC 3.2's\nCLM-trust-not-membership and CC 3.4.13's CLM-child-protection have witnesses\nto supersede to rather than sitting staged.\n\n  3.2     CLM-trust-not-membership                    check_user_target_steward_binding_admission\n  3.2     CLM-nsproc-steward-bound-predicate-trust    is_steward_bound\n  3.2     CLM-nsproc-steward-bindings-read-fold-trust steward_bindings_of\n  3.4.11  CLM-nsproc-age-band-resolution-...          engine.rs#age_band\n  3.4.13  CLM-child-protection                        age.rs#is_minor\n  3.4.13  CLM-nsproc-age-band-one-way-coarsening-...  age.rs#coarsen\n\nEVERY SYMBOL VERIFIED PRESENT BEFORE THE ROW WAS WRITTEN -- admission.rs:6784\nand :10751, engine.rs:5984 and :6059, age.rs:114 and :123 -- and then verified\nagain by evidence_cc_impl_pointers_resolve, which re-checks every src/ row\nindependently. A registry row for a symbol that does not resolve is\nsynthesized evidence, which this repo has done once and will not do again.\n\nThe two claim ids CC named on #729 are used VERBATIM; the four supporting\nsymbols carry descriptive CLM-nsproc-* ids per this file's convention. If CC's\ndesignation differs, the manifest is the designation act and CC's spelling\nwins -- flagged on the issue.\n\nRows land in the PUBLISHED section, not the UNASSIGNED one: these have CC\ndecimals, which is exactly what distinguishes the two halves of this file.\n\nThe count gate did its job: 67 -> 73 in the same commit, per its own\ninstruction. It is an EXACT count rather than a floor precisely so registry\ngrowth is a visible one-line diff -- and so a parse change that silently\nemptied the loop could not pass.\n\nNo release cut for this: evidence rows and a test constant, no code change, no\npublic surface. It rides the next feature cut (the standing don't-micro-release\nrule).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018uhFoKnaUUAcpV3kafhgjm",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-17T16:57:35-05:00",
          "tree_id": "e8842f3ba44f395757065ceca64b63bdb27fbf15",
